@startuml state-transitions
title US-13: Alert State Machine

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333

[*] --> NEW : alert evaluator publishes\nalert event to Kafka\nAPI writes initial record

NEW --> ACKNOWLEDGED : operator clicks Acknowledge\nPATCH /alerts/:alert_id\n{ status: ACKNOWLEDGED }

ACKNOWLEDGED --> RESOLVED : operator clicks Resolve\nPATCH /alerts/:alert_id\n{ status: RESOLVED }

NEW --> RESOLVED : operator skips acknowledge\nand resolves directly

RESOLVED --> [*]

note right of NEW
  alert_id = {entity_id}:{alert_type}:{window_start_ms}
  Deterministic - safe to replay from Kafka.
  Duplicate insert is a no-op via ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
end note

note right of ACKNOWLEDGED
  Records who acknowledged and when.
  Other operators see the alert is owned.
  Alert evaluator continues evaluating -
  it does not read lifecycle state.
end note

note right of RESOLVED
  Record is never deleted - it is the audit trail.
  If the anomaly recurs, a new alert_id is generated
  (new window_start_ms) - a fresh record, not a reopen.
end note

@enduml
